{title: House of the Rising Sun}
{artist: Traditional}
{key: Am}
{time: 6/8}
{tempo: 80}
{countin: 4}
# one [chord] = one bar. In 6/8 the pulse is the dotted quarter (2 per bar).

{c: Verse 1}
There is a [Am]house in [C]New Or[D]leans [F]
They [Am]call the [C]Rising [E]Sun [E]
And it's [Am]been the [C]ruin of [D]many a poor [F]boy
And [Am]God, I [E]know I'm [Am]one [E]

{c: Verse 2}
My [Am]mother [C]was a [D]tailor [F]
She [Am]sewed my [C]new blue [E]jeans [E]
My [Am]father [C]was a [D]gamblin' [F]man
[Am]Down in [E]New Or[Am]leans [E]

{c: Verse 3}
Now the [Am]only [C]thing a [D]gambler [F]needs
Is a [Am]suitcase [C]and a [E]trunk [E]
And the [Am]only [C]time he's [D]satis[F]fied
Is [Am]when he's [E]all a-[Am]drunk [E]

{c: Verse 4}
Oh [Am]mother, [C]tell your [D]children [F]
Not to [Am]do what [C]I have [E]done [E]
Spend your [Am]lives in [C]sin and [D]mise[F]ry
In the [Am]House of the [E]Rising [Am]Sun [E]

{c: Outro}
There [Am]is a [C]house in [D]New Or[F]leans
They [Am]call the [C]Rising [E]Sun [E]
